# p03 reason as a term, in the value position
#
# LinkML option: option1 union (and option1b): the slot holds either a value or a reason term.
#
# The datum's 'has value specification' points at an instance of GENEPIO:0001620 'not collected'
# instead of at a scalar value specification.
#
# A consumer can infer that no value was determined and why, as a resolvable class. They cannot
# rely on the node being a value specification: it is a datum status (a data entity), yet OBI
# 2026-07-27 declares the range of OBI:0001938 as OBI:0001933 'value specification', so a
# reasoner will classify the reason as a value specification. No disjointness prevents that, so
# it is a category error rather than an inconsistency.
#
# OBI:0002199 'reason for lack of data item' would be the OBI-native type for this node, but on
# 2026-09-14 its only descendants are OBI:0002200 'cannot be assessed determination' and three
# cancer staging codes (GX, pTX, pNX). There is no OBI term for "not collected", so GENEPIO is used.

@prefix rdf:     <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix xsd:     <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix ex:      <https://example.org/encounter/> .
@prefix BFO:     <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_> .
@prefix IAO:     <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_> .
@prefix OBI:     <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_> .
@prefix GENEPIO: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GENEPIO_> .

ex:glucoseAssay1 a owl:NamedIndividual , OBI:2100072 ;
    BFO:0000050 ex:encounter1 ;
    OBI:0000293 ex:specimen1 ;
    OBI:0000299 ex:glucoseDatum1 .

ex:glucoseDatum1 a owl:NamedIndividual , IAO:0000109 ;
    IAO:0000136 ex:specimen1 ;
    OBI:0001938 ex:reason1 .               # reason where a value specification belongs

ex:reason1 a owl:NamedIndividual , GENEPIO:0001620 .
